{"kind": "mod", "id": 2204, "name": "Deep Fried Headsets", "slug": "deep-fried-headsets", "teaser": "Bring back the oomph (Boosted headsets)", "owner_name": "shenghanzhe", "downloads": 8373, "favourites": 8, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": true, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "com.shwng.deepfriedheadsets", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Audio", "category_id": 12, "updated_at": "2026-07-28T08:00:51.000000Z", "created_at": "2025-06-27T21:28:08.000000Z", "published_at": "2026-02-01T14:40:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.0 <4.1.0", "latest_version": "1.2.0", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<p>This mod boosts and tweaks all headsets in Escape from Tarkov to make them much more powerful.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Greatly increases ambient noise reduction (quieter background sounds)</li>\n<li>Makes all headset audio much louder</li>\n<li>Boosts low, mid, and high frequencies</li>\n<li>Makes footsteps much more noticeable</li>\n<li>Slightly increases the distance at which you can hear sounds</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The goal is to make headsets feel much more effective and dramatic, so you can hear important sounds (like footsteps) more easily, like it was before in SPT 3.9.<br />\nSomewhat descriptive config file is in config\\ folder.<br />\n3.10 version pinned to the comment.</p>\n<p>Not usable for those who owns 5.1/7.1 headsets, sound becomes VERY awkward.</p>\n<p>For 2.0 stereo without any sound enhancements works fine</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://buymeacoffee.com/shengzhanzhe\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">buymeacoffee</a></p>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.0.1", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.11.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 4209, "published_at": "2025-06-29T23:40:10.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2204/deep-fried-headsets/1.0.1", "github_ur